# Lambda X-Ray Tracer

## Setup

- **Powertools Tracer:** `new Tracer({ serviceName, captureHTTPsRequests: true })`; singleton; use in handler and services
- **Trace ID:** `process.env._X_AMZN_TRACE_ID`; parse for traceId/parentId/sampled if needed for logging or external systems
- **AWS SDK:** `tracer.captureAWSv3Client(new S3Client({}))` (and similar) to capture SDK calls automatically

## Subsegments

- **Manual:** `const subsegment = segment?.addNewSubsegment('name')`; add annotations (`addAnnotation`), errors (`addError`); `subsegment?.close()` in finally
- Use for key operations (e.g. processMessage, validateUpload) to see timing and errors in service map

## Middleware

- Use Powertools tracer middleware (or Middy middleware) so handler is wrapped; ensure subsegments are closed on error paths

## Conventions

- One Tracer per service; capture SDK clients; add subsegments for important steps; include correlationId/traceId in logs

## Anti-Patterns

- Not closing subsegments; capturing sensitive data in annotations; missing error recording

**See also:** `logging-setup.mdc`, `logging-tracing-capture.mdc`, `logging-metrics-correlation.mdc`
